    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1561">

                <pb facs="1258" n="1142" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.00/393.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President has decided to have this Government supervise the registration and
                    election in Panama, and has directed this Department to designate you as
                    chairman and Colonel Goethals and the colonel commanding the regiment of
                    infantry now stationed on the Isthmus to act as a committee for supervision of
                    registration and election and for taking such suitable measures, after
                    consulting with the Government and both parties, as will secure fairness in the
                    registration and election.</p>
                <p>You will inform the Panaman Government of the foregoing and notify the leaders of
                    both parties who have communicated with you of this Government’s decision. The
                    Department is communicating with the Panaman Minister here and with the War
                    Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
